  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aqua for All PPP Innovation Program 2014 to mid-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aqua for All focuses on people at the Base of the Pyramid in African and Asian countries: those who most often lack access to water and sanitation services. Ensuring access to clean water and good sanitation is step one in empowering people with the ability to improve their lives.5 x WATER AND POVERTY1. Water-poor communities are typically also economically poor, trapped in a cycle of poverty.2. Education suffers when children, sick of polluted water-related ailments, miss school.3. Economic opportunities are routinely lost to the impacts of rampant illnesses.4. Acquiring water from far away requires valuable time better spent going to school and/or working.5. Children and women are generally more vulnerable to disease and loss of opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Aqua for All, established in 2002, aims to improve the access to safe water and sanitation for people at the Base of the Pyramid in developing countries by supporting innovation and public private partnerships (PPPs). The PPP Innovation Program is a continuation of the previous Building Bridges Program. The PPP Innovation program consists of 2 core activities:1) The continuation of a fund for PPP initiatives for WASH-services (PPP-Small)2) Management of the VIA Water fund to stimulate small scale innovations in 7 African countries.Originally the period of the PPP Innovation Program was 1 November 2014 - 31 October 2018. A subsidy of 20 million euro was granted by DGIS. This subsidy of 20 million would (at least) be matched with 20 million contribution by others.A &apos;supplement&apos; request was submitted and approved by DGIS for additional subsidy of 4.55 million and extension of the project period until 30 June 2019</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of the PPP innovation project is&apos; to contribute from the result-oriented innovation and Public Private Partnerships (PPPs) to the realization of the water and sanitation related Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and within that the breakthrough on a number of urgent problems (&apos;pressing needs&apos;).</narrative>
  </description>
